# Motion

An animation catalogue that assaults motion-sensitive visitors is badly built.

## Site chrome

- Contact sheet under `prefers-reduced-motion`: static first frames + one “Play the sheet” control
- Per-plate play remains available regardless
- Never rely on motion alone to communicate state (locks, copy success, filters)

## Specimens

Every new specimen CSS must include **both** triggers:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { /* animation: none */ }
[data-force-reduced-motion="true"] /* same */ { /* animation: none */ }
```

Keep the static effect visible when motion stops. Playground starter seed already satisfies this — preserve it on export.
